  "notes": "{同意|どうい} means both \"agreement\" (sharing the same opinion) and \"consent\" (giving permission). Composed of {同|どう} (same) + {意|い} (intention).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {同意|どうい}する: to agree, to consent\n- {同意|どうい}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{得|え}る→得る：02014_eru⟧: to obtain consent\n- {同意|どうい}{書|しょ}: consent form\n- {同意|どうい}なく: without consent\n- 〜に{同意|どうい}する: to agree to/with ~\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{合意|ごうい}→合意：05093_goui⟧: mutual agreement (emphasizes both parties agreeing together)\n- ⟦{賛成|さんせい}→賛成：02829_sansei⟧: approval, support (for a proposal or plan)\n- ⟦{承諾|しょうだく}→承諾：12778_shoudaku⟧: consent, acceptance (responding to a request — more formal)\n- ⟦{同感|どうかん}→同感：18240_doukan⟧: sharing the same feeling (\"I feel the same way\")\n\nREGISTER:\nNeutral to formal. {同意|どうい}{書|しょ} (consent form) is common in medical and legal contexts.",
